Window placement across outputs.

- A fullscreen X11 window is shown on the output its own geometry is on,
  not on the output the pointer is on.  Wine puts fullscreen games on the
  X11 primary output; shown on another, they stayed black or got the mouse
  offset (BFME), as they kept drawing for the output they asked for.
- Other new windows (without a parent) open on the output their app's
  windows were last closed on, if it is still connected, and otherwise where
  the user is, as before.  The outputs are kept by app id in
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/cosmic-comp/window-outputs.  Windows started from the
  dock or a launcher carry the workspace they were started on (activation
  token); that one is kept only if it is on the remembered output.

